A||||9||Jay in Atlanta||Drive Your Fiero to Work Day!||||10||
Z||000000||Jay in Atlanta||08-10-2001||10:10 PM||||It's time to reiterate that Monday, August 13th is the new Drive Your Fiero to Work Day!  This commemorates the sad passing of this one-of-a-kind American car; the last Fiero rolled off the line on August 12, 1988.<P>Corvette owners have a Drive to Work Day, and now we do, too, every 2nd Monday in August.<P>Get those show cars and even the junky Fieros out of the garage and drive them to work or school!  And if you already have a daily driver Fiero--like me!--just make sure it's on the road on Monday.<P>Looking forward to seeing ALL the Fieros out there on the 13th!<P>~Jay<BR>red '85 SE 5-Speed||||reg||10
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||08-10-2001||10:42 PM||||Cool, hopefully, I get to see a bunch of Fieros on my birthday.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||08-10-2001||10:50 PM||||I don't think I can fit a floor sander, edger, compressor, air nailer, miter saw, table saw, buffer, a can of extremely flamable floor sealer and 5 gallons of polyurethane into the trunk, but I will drive it on Monday after work. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
